  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 5 - Before the development is commenced a scheme for soundproofing between lower floor flat and upper floor flat shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - The roof light hereby permitted shall be flush with the existing plane of the roof.",
    "Condition : 7 - The application for the conversion of the existing premises to provide a two-bed flat at first floor and a two-bed maisonette at second and roof level incorporating the erection of two rear roof extensions, as shown on drawing numbers 059/A051 (Revision 03), 059/A050 (Revision 03), 059/A070 (Revision 03) and 059/A60 (Revision 03), received 28 February 2007; 59/A100 (Rev 04), received 23 April 2007; and 059/A101 (Rev 05B) and 059/A102 (Revision 05B), 059/A170 (Revision 04B) and 059/A160 (Revision 04B), received 24 April 2007, is recommended for approval as the converted property is of an appropriate size and configuration for use as two units and its use as flats would not unduly harm the amenity of neighbours or adversely affect the character of the area The proposed rear roof extensions and single roof light to the front roof slope would be compatible with the scale and form of the original building and the adjacent roof extension and they would maintain the amenity of neighbouring properties and the character of the street scene. Therefore the proposed development complies with the relevant London Borough of Hounslow Unitary Development Plan 2003 policies; ENV-B.1.1 All New Development, H.3.4 Conversions of Houses to Flats, H.4.1 Housing Standards and Guidelines, H.6.4 Extensions and Alterations, T.1.4 Car and Cycle Parking and Servicing Facilities for Developments and the Supplementary Planning Guidance."
  ],
